WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:11.590
BioSync is a governed, multimodal precision-intelligence platform designed to turn fragmented molecular and laboratory data into structured, traceable, human-reviewed clinical and research outputs.

2
00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:19.484
The platform brings genetics, metabolomics, laboratory data, and cross-domain analysis into one coherent environment.

3
00:00:19.484 --> 00:00:27.706
Its visual language mirrors that architecture: distinct scientific domains, connected without erasing their individual evidence boundaries.

4
00:00:28.406 --> 00:00:40.702
After sign-in, the clinical workspace gives the professional a concise operational view: patients, active cases, submitted tests, pending review, reports, and the next action that requires attention.

5
00:00:41.402 --> 00:00:47.771
Every case, examination, interpretation, and report remains connected to a single longitudinal identity.

6
00:00:47.771 --> 00:00:53.650
This demonstration uses a fictional patient created inside an isolated test environment.

7
00:00:54.350 --> 00:01:02.629
A new case begins by selecting or creating the patient, identifying the responsible professional, and choosing the scientific domain.

8
00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:06.550
This establishes provenance before any molecular file is interpreted.

9
00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:11.559
Raw genotype data is attached to the existing case.

10
00:01:11.559 --> 00:01:16.348
The pipeline resolves observed genotypes against a curated canonical registry.

11
00:01:16.348 --> 00:01:23.530
Only raw-data-supported findings may enter the clinical projection; absent, unresolved, and ambiguous evidence remains explicit.

12
00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:28.470
Generated reports remain versioned and attached to their source case.

13
00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:33.982
The same canonical renderer and components govern real reports and controlled visual baselines.

14
00:01:34.682 --> 00:01:43.703
Metabolomics uses a source-independent canonical model with aliases, unit normalization, confidence states, pathways, and clinical patterns.

15
00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:47.650
Source-specific inputs are normalized without losing provenance.

16
00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:53.729
Cross-domain convergence begins only after each domain has resolved its own truth.

17
00:01:53.729 --> 00:02:01.798
It classifies support, conflict, convergence, or insufficient evidence without allowing one domain to manufacture another domain's missing data.

18
00:02:02.498 --> 00:02:12.538
Automation may gather evidence and prepare candidate structures, but no association becomes canonical patient-facing content without an explicit, recorded human decision.

19
00:02:13.238 --> 00:02:16.775
Capabilities are granted explicitly by tenant and role.

20
00:02:16.775 --> 00:02:22.966
The interface distinguishes available tools from features outside the current plan without inferring access.

21
00:02:23.666 --> 00:02:33.154
Settings, permissions, feature controls, and audit structures make operational responsibility visible while preserving fail-closed behavior and professional oversight.

22
00:02:33.954 --> 00:02:40.919
BioSync is not yet publicly available to health professionals, and no public release date has been announced.

23
00:02:40.919 --> 00:02:45.426
As a multi-omic platform, it is continuously evolving and being updated.

24
00:02:45.426 --> 00:02:53.210
The next domain now in development is microbiota, extending the platform's architecture while preserving traceability, governance, and human review.
